# Generated by Cargo: each workspace root's build output — the repo's, app's
# and tools/lint's. Anchored, because a bare `target` or `debug` also matches a
# module of that name, and an ignored source file passes every gate on the disk
# that has it and is missing from the push (PR #872's `cache/`; #1229).
# `tools/lint`'s `ignored` rule fails on any code file a rule here swallows.
/debug/
/target/
/app/target/
/tools/lint/target/
# A crate's own tests run from its folder, so a relative `target/` they write
# scratch under lands there.
/crates/*/target/

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Bytecode from the signal renderers' tests under .github/scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Secrets — .env.example is committed, real credentials never are
.env

# The web front-end's installed packages and its build output. `bun.lock` is
# committed; what it resolves to, and what `vite build` writes, are not.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
# What a Playwright run leaves: a failed flow's trace and screenshot (#898).
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# Rebuildable per-project cache inside *.scor/ project directories, wherever a
# project sits (a test's, a fixture's). Never a source folder of that name:
# `cache/` alone also matched `crates/render/src/page/cache/`, so a new file
# there was silently left out of a commit while the coder's own build, which
# had it on disk, passed (PR #872).
cache/
!crates/**/src/**/cache/
!app/src/**/cache/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Snapshot comparison leaves these beside the references when a panel changed.
# The reference is committed; what a failing run produced is not, and neither
# is the reference a blessing run replaced — `.old.png` is the picture that was
# just superseded, which is a thing to look at once and never a thing to keep.
*.new.png
*.diff.png
*.old.png

# Claude Code's per-clone state. `skills/` is committed — the working protocols
# travel with the repo or they are not protocols — and so are `settings.json`
# and `hooks/`, the cloud container's setup (#722). Nothing else here is:
# `worktrees/` is scratch checkouts measured in gigabytes, and
# `settings.local.json` is one machine's permissions.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/

# The landing page's project (#904): a baked score is rebuilt by `scorsese
# synth bake`, the same bytes every time, so only the recipe is kept.
web/landing/*.scor/generated/

# Terraform's provider download. Its lockfile is committed; the state lives in
# the state bucket, never here (deploy/terraform/tf), and the override `tf`
# writes to reach an old local state is deleted when it exits.
deploy/terraform/*/.terraform/
deploy/terraform/*/tf_local_override.tf
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
